.Dd August 31, 2026
.Dt CB-CONFIG 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cb-config
.Nd cb's config.json format and template DSL
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr cb 1 Ns 's
user config is a single JSON file, by default
.Pa ~/.config/cb/config.json
.Pq override with Ev CB_CONFIG_FILE ,
honoring
.Ev XDG_CONFIG_HOME
if set.
It is user-authored and
.Nm cb
never rewrites it \(em mutable state lives in the separate event log
instead
.Pq see Xr cb 1 Ns 's Sx FILES .
Every key is optional; an absent key falls back to its built-in
default, shown throughout this page.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "workDir": [{"var": "HOME"}, "/work"],
  "projects": { "baseDir": [{"var": "workDir"}, "/.base"] },
  "branches": {
    "name": [{"var": "USER"}, "/", {"date": "YYYYMMDD.HHmmss"}, "/",
             {"join": {"delimiter": "--",
                       "elements": [{"var": "ticket"}, {"var": "worktree-key"}]}}]
  }
}
.Ed
.Sh THE TEMPLATE DSL
Every string-valued config key documented below is actually a
.Em template :
a JSON array whose elements are rendered and concatenated in order.
A plain JSON string element is emitted literally; three object forms
are also recognized:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic {"var": Ar name }
Resolves
.Ar name
in this order: a config-defined global
.Pq currently only Ic workDir ,
then a per-command value available in the current context
.Pq e.g. Ic ticket , Ic worktree-key , Ic projectDir , Ic worktreeDir ,
then an environment variable of the same name.
An unresolved
.Ar name
renders as empty.
.It Ic {"date": Ar format }
Renders the current time in UTC using
.Ar format ,
a string built from the tokens
.Ic YYYY MM DD HH mm ss ;
any other character passes through literally.
.It Ic {"join": {"delimiter": Ar d , "elements": [ Ns Ar ... Ns ]}}
Renders each element the same way, drops any that render empty, and
joins the survivors with
.Ar d .
Used so an absent
.Ic ticket
does not leave a stray delimiter in a branch name.
.El
.Pp
A template that references itself, directly or through another
template, is a configuration error
.Pq Ic CyclicVariable .
.Sh TOP-LEVEL KEYS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic workDir
Where worktrees live, absent a project-specific override.
Default:
.Ic [{"var": "HOME"}, "/work"] .
.It Ic projects.baseDir
Default directory for
.Ic cb mkproject Ar key
when no explicit
.Ar dir
is given:
.Ar baseDir Ns / Ns Ar key .
Default:
.Ic [{"var": "workDir"}, "/.base"] .
.It Ic branches.name
Default branch name for
.Ic cb mk ,
absent
.Fl Fl branch-name .
Rendered with
.Ic ticket
and
.Ic worktree-key
available.
Default renders
.Ar $USER Ns / Ns Ar YYYYMMDD.HHmmss Ns / Ns Op Ar ticket-- Ns Ar worktree-key .
.El
.Sh BRANCH-TO-DIRECTORY MAPPING
A rendered branch name becomes a worktree directory name by a fixed,
one-way rule, not itself configurable:
.Ic /
becomes
.Ic -- ,
and any other character outside
.Ic A-Za-z0-9._-
collapses a run of such characters into a single
.Ic - .
.Sh POST-CREATE HOOKS
.Ic cb mk
can copy files from the project checkout into the new worktree and run
setup commands immediately after creating it, unless
.Fl Fl no-hooks
is passed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
  "worktrees": {
    "copy": [".env", ".env.local"],
    "onCreate": ["pnpm install"]
  },
  "projects": {
    "overrides": {
      "myproj": { "worktrees": { "onCreate": ["make dev-setup"] } }
    }
  }
}
.Ed
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic worktrees.copy
A list of template-DSL entries, each rendering to a path relative to
the worktree root.
.Ic projectDir
and
.Ic worktreeDir
are additionally available here, alongside
.Ic ticket
and
.Ic worktree-key .
For each entry,
.Xr cb 1
copies that path from the project checkout into the same relative path
in the new worktree.
An absolute path or one containing
.Ic ..
is rejected; a missing source file is a warning, not a failure.
.It Ic worktrees.standalone
Boolean, default
.Ic false .
When
.Ic true ,
.Ic cb mk
creates a standalone
.Ic git clone --local
instead of a linked
.Xr git-worktree 1 ,
as if
.Fl Fl standalone
had been passed; overridden in either direction by an explicit
.Fl Fl standalone No / Fl Fl no-standalone
flag.
See
.Xr cb 1 Ns 's
.Cm mk
for the trade-offs.
.It Ic worktrees.onCreate
A list of template-DSL entries, each rendering to a shell command.
Each command runs via
.Ic $SHELL -c
in the new worktree, output inherited, with
.Ev CB_PROJECT_DIR ,
.Ev CB_PROJECT_KEY ,
.Ev CB_WORKTREE_DIR ,
.Ev CB_WORKTREE_KEY ,
.Ev CB_BRANCH ,
.Ev CB_BASE ,
and
.Pq if set Ev CB_TICKET
set in its environment.
A failing command stops the remaining
.Ic onCreate
commands but leaves the worktree in place.
.It Ic projects.overrides. Ns Ar key Ns Ic .worktrees
When present for a project
.Ar key ,
.Em replaces
.Pq does not merge with
that project's global
.Ic worktrees.copy ,
.Ic worktrees.onCreate ,
and
.Ic worktrees.standalone
entirely.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cb 1 ,
.Xr cb-review 7
